1. e4 e5 2. d4 exd4 3. Qxd4 { Centre Game is a strange opening choice. White loses an important tempo in the opening and develops his pieces awkwardly. Black can successfully fight for more than equality. -KEY- } Nc6 4. Qc4 ( { This is much less known than } 4. Qe3 { but it's not without its points. } ) 
Nf6 5. Nc3 Bb4 { Just developing actively. } 6. Bd2 O-O 7. O-O-O a5 $1 ( { This is more accurate than natural } 7... Re8 8. f3 { We need to act quickly, otherwise White can create an unpleasant bind with f3 and g4. With our move we protect the bishop and prepare ...Ne5 ...Re8 and ...d5. } ) 
8. a3 Bxc3 9. Bxc3 b5 $15 { Of course we need to play vigorously once we gave up the bishop pair. } 
